From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] omcproxy: initialize downlink scope before querier replay

querier_attach() synchronously announces existing group state after linking
the user to the querier. Its callback reads the downlink scope, which is
still zero if flags are copied only after attachment. Copy the configured
scope before invoking that producer; allocation, attachment and error
cleanup retain their native owners.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/src/proxy.c
+++ b/src/proxy.c
@@ -191,10 +191,10 @@ int proxy_set(int uplink, const int down
 		if (mrib_attach_user(&downlink->mrib, downlinks[i], NULL))
 			goto downlink_err2;
 
+		/* Attaching can immediately announce existing group state. */
+		downlink->flags = proxy->flags;
 		if (querier_attach(&downlink->iface, &proxy->querier, downlinks[i], proxy_trigger))
 			goto downlink_err1;
-
-		downlink->flags = proxy->flags;
 		continue;
 
 downlink_err1:
